# op25 (boatbod/op25 @ da5374d), seven independent changes; apply in a clean checkout: git apply
#   1. (upstream since da5374d: boatbod/op25 #306, the op25_crypt_algs destructor fix)
#   2. apps/tx/op25_c4fm_mod.py: transfer_function_nxdn() and _nxdn_tx() accept the rate_multiplier argument
#      that c4fm_taps.generate() passes to every generator (NXDN filter taps failed with a TypeError)
#   3. DMR: the color code as a trailing byte of the CACH SLC, CSBK, voice LC, terminator LC and embedded LC
#      messages (dmr_slot.cc/.h, dmr_cai.cc)
#   4. P25 Phase 1 TX: a settable NAC and Link Control (vocoder set_nac() / set_lc(); the defaults keep the
#      fixed NAC 0x293 and preset LC)
#   5. dmr_ms_tx_bb: a DMR mobile-station voice transmitter block (bursts a repeater's receiver accepts)
#   6. dmr_bs_tx_bb: embedded LC in voice bursts B-E and a null embedded field with the EMB in burst F (it sent
#      fragments in B, C, E, F and an all-zero burst D, so no receiver could assemble the LC: no TG / source)
#   7. dmr_bs_tx_bb: a disabled timeslot sends idle data bursts (slot type: CC + data type 9) instead of the
#      silence encoder's AMBE under the data sync, which receivers decoded as garbage headers and voice
#   8. dmr receive: the color code learned on one timeslot also applies to the other (dmr_slot::adopt_cc),
#      so a call with no data burst on its own slot (no voice LC header) still has its EMBs accepted
# Upstream-Status: 1 merged (#306); open on boatbod/op25 dev: 2 (#307), 3 (#308), 6 (#309), 4 (#310); 7 (after 6) and 8 (after 3)
# next; 5 on hold
